#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# differential_separant

#% text
# `differential_separant(p, u, x)` gives the separant of the differential polynomial `p` in the functions `u` of `x`: its derivative with respect to its leader. Every proper derivative of `p` is linear in its own leader, with the separant as coefficient.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The ranking is `ranking: orderly` (the default) or `ranking: elimination`, as for `differential_leader`. The separant is 0 when `p` contains no derivative of the functions.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
differential_separant(y'(x)^2 - 4*y(x), y, x)
#% output
#= 2*y'(x)

#% text
# The derivative of `p` is linear in `y''`, with the separant as coefficient:

#% cell
d(y'(x)^2 - 4*y(x), x)
#% output
#= -4*y'(x) + 2*y'(x)*y''(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `differential_leader`, `differential_initial`, `differential_reduce`
